    "lineage": "",
    "mech_note": "Ancestral Warchief: summon a stationary ancestral totem that performs your equipped melee skill (slam) independently while you stand nearby. The player is a COACH: positioning yourself adjacent to the totem grants it a damage buff (melee proximity bonus); placing 2-3 totems (Ancestral Bond or Hierophant) multiplies output. The totems inherit weapon damage and slam type from the player's equipped weapon. The player's role is placement (drop totems on the pack, maintain proximity buff) rather than pressing attack. Chieftain ascendancy (Ngamahu's totem fire damage, endurance charge generation) made this the canonical fire-totem melee build; Atlas passive tree synergies elevated it for endgame bossing. Long-running viability across many leagues as a safe, cheap, reliable starter. The 'melee outsourced to deployed ancestors' archetype.",
    "mint": 0,
